 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545764,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A toaster oven is labeled as 2,000 W. How much would it cost to warm leftovers from a meal for 15 minutes if the electric rate is 12 cents per kilowatt-hour?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{1,000}}{{{\\rm{2000\\ watts}}}} = 0.5{\\rm{\\ hours\\ to\\ use\\ 1\\ kW}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Time in use: 15 minutes</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"15{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{minutes}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\rm{\\ hour}}}}{{60\\cancel{{{\\rm{minutes}}}}}}} \\right) = 0.25{\\rm{\\ hours}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use the knowledge that it takes 0.25 hours and it costs 12 cents per kilowatt-hour.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.25{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{hours}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{kW}}}}}}{{0.5{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{hour}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{\\$ 0.12}}{{1{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{kW}}}}}}} \\right) \\approx {\\rm{ \\$ 0}}{\\rm{.06}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The refrigerator will cost $0.06 for 15 minutes.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$0.06"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
